  "notes": [
    "All timing control/value offsets and ranges are taken from the AMD CBS and AMD Overclocking IFR extracted from this BIOS.",
    "AOD timing gate is AodSetupRpl[0x3C]; CBS timing gate is AmdSetupRPL[0x116].",
    "AOD-over-CBS precedence is not established for this MSI BIOS. If both menus are Manual, the resolver reports unknown.",
    "MSI Setup declares A-XMP selectors at 0x595/0x6F9 and EXPO selectors at 0x596/0x6FA. The two conditional UI groups are not yet resolved to a single active selector; raw values are diagnostic only.",
    "The AOD speed selector at 0x3A is an unnamed numeric IFR field. Its MSI-specific write semantics are not established; AOD Speed is not inferred from it.",
    "The external StdDefaults NVRAM block contains AmdSetupRPL but no AodSetupRpl default entry. AOD IFR declares AodSetupRpl with size 0x320; runtime visibility must be checked on hardware.",
    "Comparison with 7D75v1E5 (2024-01-25) confirms that AMD CBS/AOD IFR matches exactly. MSI Setup increased from 0x7C2 to 0x7C4 in 1E0; EXPO/A-XMP and Memory Try It offsets stay the same.",
    "MSI's own Setup has an independent DRAM Frequency menu at 0x51B/0x68C, High-Efficiency Mode and Memory Try It; this first resolver must not label timings/Speed as Auto merely because CBS/AOD gate bytes are Auto."
  ]
